  "In February 1917 (March, New Style) a revolution overthrew Russia's imperial government; in October (November) a second placed the Bolsheviks in power. [[c-ussr-1917]] In the Civil War of 1918-20 the Red Army defended the new government against Russian and foreign anti-Bolshevik armies. A small British force landed at Murmansk in March 1918, and Japanese troops landed at Vladivostok in April. [[c-ussr-civilwar]] In March 1921 the 10th Party Congress introduced the New Economic Policy: peasants could own and farm their land, and most farming, retail trade and small industry were in private hands, while the state kept heavy industry, transport, banking and foreign trade. [[c-ussr-nep]]",
  "Stalin ended the NEP in 1928-29 by forcibly collectivizing agriculture. [[c-ussr-nep]] The famine that followed killed at least 5 million people across the USSR between 1931 and 1934, among them, according to a study by a team of Ukrainian demographers, at least 3.9 million Ukrainians. [[c-ussr-famine]] Ukraine suffered measures of its own: farms, villages and whole towns were blacklisted and denied food, and peasants were forbidden to leave the republic in search of it. [[c-ussr-blacklists]] Later Stalin suppressed the census of 1937. [[c-ussr-census1937]]",
